cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its artifacts, cite it as below. A specific .urna file is identified by its file_hash, listed in release/v0.3/<profile>/SHA256SUMS. Its content_hash identifies the content (text and vectors), which the releases share, and is what a urna:// citation resolves in any of them; both are read with urna inspect --json and recorded in CITATION_KEY. Cite Urna, the engine that builds and reads the files, and Scryfall, the source of the cards, as listed under references. Licenses differ per material: the code and results are MIT, the card images and text are Wizards of the Coast's (see the License section of the README)."
type: dataset
title: "mtg-urna-benchmark"
version: 0.3.2
date-released: 2026-09-12
repository-code: "https://github.com/brennercruvinel/mtg-urna-benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: Cruvinel
    given-names: Brenner
    affiliation: Hoff Research
    email: brenner@hoffresearch.com
abstract: "compression and retrieval benchmark of the 38,627-card magic: the gathering image corpus packed into single-file .urna containers with the urna engine: av1, avif and jpeg xl media variants, lossless batteries, inter-frame ordering over same-artwork reprints, an all-intra codec battery at matched ssimulacra2, and retrieval-only profiles measured on identity, embedding drift and text-to-image hit@k against a 3.975 GB jpeg source."
keywords:
  - image compression
  - set redundancy
  - album coding
  - av1
  - avif
  - jpeg xl
  - ssimulacra2
  - image retrieval
  - embeddings
  - vector database
  - single-file container
  - magic the gathering
  - scryfall
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: "sha256:cb8fdf8f13fa50f93969de7603386f1c2b117a5e4946c60ac9894a3c5a1f062b"
    description: "content_hash of every full-corpus file since 2026-09-12: the v0.3 archive and neardup releases (rebuilt) and the three experiment 13 candidates (av1 crf40, av1 crf50, avif q48)"
  - type: other
    value: "sha256:c993ceda5b42749487ebd20df7f9dc10e321f3f6099dc73e8008f6524b98a582"
    description: "historical: content_hash of the v0.3 neardup and archive releases as first built under the spellbook name; replaced by the 2026-09-12 rebuild"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Urna"
    abstract: "Offline-first vector database that stores text chunks, embeddings, source spans, indices and a search contract in a single .urna file. The v0.3 files were built with its forge before the rename from nest (built_with in each CITATION_KEY)."
    authors:
      - family-names: Cruvinel
        given-names: Brenner
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3079-8829"
        affiliation: Hoff Research
    repository-code: "https://github.com/hoffresearch/urna"
    url: "https://urna.dev"
    license: MIT
  - type: database
    title: "Scryfall bulk data"
    authors:
      - name: Scryfall
    url: "https://scryfall.com/docs/api/bulk-data"
    notes: "Card data and images. The images and card text are property of Wizards of the Coast."
